WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.178
HKDSE 2026, Paper 1, Question 7. Topic: Profit, Discount & Percentage. This is the full worked solution in English.

2
00:00:11.598 --> 00:00:24.769
A profit of 162 is made by selling a ring at a discount of 15 percent on its marked price. The marked price of the ring is 270 above its cost. Find the percentage profit.

3
00:00:25.189 --> 00:00:29.893
STEP 1 — define variables.

4
00:00:30.053 --> 00:00:37.316
Let M equals marked price and C equals cost price. M equals C plus 270.

5
00:00:37.736 --> 00:00:42.723
STEP 2 — express the selling price.

6
00:00:42.883 --> 00:00:55.134
Key rule: Discount. selling price equals (1 minus d percent) times marked price. A 15 percent discount means the ring sells at 0.85M.

7
00:00:55.294 --> 00:01:03.291
A 15 percent discount means the ring sells at 85 percent of the marked price: SP equals 0.85M.

8
00:01:03.711 --> 00:01:08.757
STEP 3 — use the profit information.

9
00:01:08.917 --> 00:01:19.296
SP-C equals 162 which gives 0.85M-C equals 162 Substitute M equals C plus 270.

10
00:01:19.456 --> 00:01:41.486
0.85(C plus 270)-C equals 162 0.85C plus 229.5 minus C equals 162 which gives minus 0.15C equals minus 67.5 which gives C equals 450 Hence M equals 450 plus 270 equals.

11
00:01:41.646 --> 00:01:49.088
720, and SP equals 0.85 times 720 equals 612.

12
00:01:49.508 --> 00:01:53.941
STEP 4 — percentage profit.

13
00:01:54.101 --> 00:02:08.003
Key rule: Percentage Profit. profit percent equals profit over cost times 100 percent. Profit is 162 on a cost of 450, so the percentage profit is 36 percent.

14
00:02:08.163 --> 00:02:16.054
Percentage profit equals 162 over 450 times 100 percent equals 36 percent.

15
00:02:16.474 --> 00:02:21.086
So the answer is: The percentage profit is 36 percent.

16
00:02:21.506 --> 00:02:30.420
That completes HKDSE 2026 Paper 1 Question 7. Every step shown here matches the worked solution on the page.
